  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ahsanbhai Shakeelbhai Ansari vs State Of Gujarat & on 5 May, 2017 Author: A.G.Uraizee Bench: A.G.Uraizee R/Cr.Ra/440/2017 Order",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "Learned advocate Mr. Kishan H. Daiya for the applicant submits that there is clear violation of Section 11(1)(a) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act and before taking the sample, the intention that the sample was taken for analysis is not disclosed. He further submits that the notice as contemplated under Section 13(2) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act was also not served upon the applicant and therefore, he submits that there are violations of mandatory provisions of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act. Hence, according to him, present application requires consideration.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned advocate Mr. Kishan H. Daiya for the applicant submits that there is clear violation of Section 11(1)(a) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act and before taking the sample, the intention that the sample was taken for analysis is not disclosed. He further submits that the notice as contemplated under Section 13(2) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act was also not served upon the applicant and therefore, he submits that there are violations of mandatory provisions of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act. Hence, according to him, present application requires consideration.",
